From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:53:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: HAVi gives the configuration that matches a template
 best

HGraphicsDevice, HVideoDevice and HBackgroundDevice.getBestConfiguration()
compared each configuration's match() with a score that never changed
from -1: every configuration that the template did not refuse replaced
the one before, and the last of them came back, not the best. And
HScreenConfigTemplate.matchPreference() scored a PREFERRED or
PREFERRED_NOT preference 0 whatever the configuration had, so a disc's
preferences were not looked at. With the seven configurations a device
has (1920x1080 first, 960x540 last), a template that asks for 1920x1080,
or for 1280x720, as a preference and not as a requirement got 960x540,
and so did one that cares for nothing, which should get the default
configuration, the first.

Now each method keeps the highest score, and the first configuration
that has it on a tie (the default one first). A PREFERRED preference adds
1 where the configuration has it, PREFERRED_NOT where it has not; REQUIRED
and REQUIRED_NOT are as before. A configuration that a template refuses
(-1) is never chosen, as before. On a profile 5 (3D) player the
template that HVideoDevice hands to getS3DConfiguration() (libbluray-9106)
is the one of that best score, whose 3D mode the configuration reports.
The fault was found in CroqueMr's
libbluray (CroqueMr/libbluray-cb1 4b4d3a9052, after CE Canary); it is in
libbluray's master too.

Checked with a host test of the classes (tools/regress/bdj, JDK 8, the
jar built with the command of the image's build): 11 checks, among them
the video device of a 3D player with two templates; without the patch,
9 of them fail (each gets 960x540).
---
 .../java/org/havi/ui/HBackgroundDevice.java   | 19 ++++++++++++++----
 .../bdj/java/org/havi/ui/HGraphicsDevice.java | 19 ++++++++++++++----
 .../org/havi/ui/HScreenConfigTemplate.java    |  5 +++++
 .../bdj/java/org/havi/ui/HVideoDevice.java    | 20 ++++++++++++++-----
 4 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/havi/ui/HBackgroundDevice.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/havi/ui/HBackgroundDevice.java
index 4a31032..52ffa7b 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/havi/ui/HBackgroundDevice.java
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/havi/ui/HBackgroundDevice.java
@@ -55,21 +55,32 @@ public class HBackgroundDevice extends HScreenDevice {
     }
 
     public HBackgroundConfiguration getBestConfiguration(HBackgroundConfigTemplate hbct) {
+        /* Hades: the configuration that matches best, the first of them on a tie (the default one
+           first); one that the template refuses (-1) is never chosen */
         int score = -1;
         HBackgroundConfiguration hbc = null;
-        for (int i = 0; i < hbcArray.length; i++)
-            if (hbct.match(hbcArray[i]) > score)
+        for (int i = 0; i < hbcArray.length; i++) {
+            int s = hbct.match(hbcArray[i]);
+            if (s > score) {
+                score = s;
                 hbc = hbcArray[i];
+            }
+        }
         return hbc;
     }
 
     public HBackgroundConfiguration getBestConfiguration(HBackgroundConfigTemplate hbcta[]) {
+        /* Hades: the configuration that matches one of the templates best, the first on a tie */
         int score = -1;
         HBackgroundConfiguration hbc = null;
         for (int i = 0; i < hbcArray.length; i++)
-            for (int j = 0; j < hbcta.length; j++)
-                if (hbcta[j].match(hbcArray[i]) > score)
+            for (int j = 0; j < hbcta.length; j++) {
+                int s = hbcta[j].match(hbcArray[i]);
+                if (s > score) {
+                    score = s;
                     hbc = hbcArray[i];
+                }
+            }
         return hbc;
     }
 
